    "derived_from": "cSlope verification problem V089 (MIT License), https://github.com/ZilanCiftci/cslope",
    "notes": [
      "Outline from commercial program A's printed slip-surface endpoints (Fig. 65.2): 45 ft high, crest ±15 ft, toes ±200 ft; the pool line ends on the upstream face at x = 117.778 ft. From there the line follows that face down to its toe, so no water ponds on that side (a line that ends is otherwise continued level to the edge); the circle is on the other face, and its FOS is the same either way. commercial program A GLE 2.744, USACE 2.71 (Bishop).",
      "Table 65.1 prints φ = 35° for the embankment, which gives 3.10–3.14; φ = 25° (USACE fig. 4-2) reproduces commercial program A's results and is used.",
      "program D 2.725 / 2.748 on the earlier 50 ft outline (crest ±17 ft, toes ±217 ft), where cSlope gave 2.724 / 2.747.",
      "cSlope fija options.tolerance = 0.001 (tolerancia del solver) en sus checks; no se importa: ogs usa analysis.tolerance = 1e-05.",
      "agua embalsada: la piezométrica pasa sobre el terreno; ogs la incluye en todas las versiones, con su peso y su empuje horizontal y sin sismo (F5.3); cSlope la carga con `followBoundary: false`."
    ]
